Subject: generic_vhost_user: negotiate and serve the shared memory window

A vhost-user backend can only expose host memory to the guest through a
virtio shared memory region: the VMM allocates a host window, exports it
as a dedicated PCI BAR, and maps backend-provided fds into it on request.
cloud-hypervisor v53 has the plumbing (the `cache` field, get_shm_regions,
userspace_mappings) but never negotiates SHMEM, never asks the backend for
sizes, and device_manager always passes `None` -- so the window never
exists.

For Leandro this is not optional. The very first mapping CUDA needs is
TURING_USERMODE_A (the doorbell), 64 KiB of MMIO on the card. It cannot
come from guest RAM, and routing its writes through the command stream
would turn a zero-roundtrip submission path into one roundtrip per
submission.

Changes:
- Advertise VhostUserProtocolFeatures::SHMEM. When the backend acks it,
  call GET_SHMEM_CONFIG and remember the requested region sizes; expose
  them via GenericVhostUser::shmem_sizes().
- device_manager: allocate one host window covering all regions (rounded
  up to a power of two, as the BAR requires), back it with an anonymous
  PROT_NONE mapping, register it as a KVM userspace mapping, and hand it
  to the device via the new set_cache().
- Implement shmem_map/shmem_unmap on the backend request handler. Both
  bounds-check the request against the window before touching anything --
  a backend is not trusted to stay inside it. Unmap restores an anonymous
  PROT_NONE region rather than leaving a hole.
- pci_device: skip zero-length shared memory regions when emitting PCI
  capabilities. The shmid IS the region index, so a device that needs a
  specific id (virtio-gpu wants VIRTIO_GPU_SHM_ID_HOST_VISIBLE = 1) must
  pad the list -- and PCI capability space is tight enough that an unused
  22-byte entry overflows it ("capability of size 22 doesn't fit").
- The device's `cache` field drops its second tuple element. It was an
  MmapRegion nobody ever read, and it cannot be filled at all when the
  same region is already held through the Arc in VirtioSharedMemoryList.

Measured with this project as the backend: guest reports
"+host_visible" and "Host memory window: 0x3fffe0000000 +0x10000000",
creates a HOST3D blob, and reads back the pattern the host wrote into the
memfd it mapped into the window.

